Looking at the `remove` method, the comment states that a null return value implies the key was not present before, or it was mapped to null.

The observer methods available are `containsKey` and `get`. I use `\old` to refer to pre-removal state.

<code>assert \result == null => (!\old(this.containsKey(key)) || \old(this.get(key)) == null);</code>
