Looking at the comment, I need to express: if the returned value is null, then either the key was not in the map before removal, or the value previously mapped to the key was null.

The available observer methods are `containsKey` and `get`. I use `\old` to refer to the state before the removal.

<code>assert \result == null => (!\old(this.containsKey(key)) || \old(this.get(key)) == null);</code>
--------------------
